& [SJS]
  + Situation: inspect is intended as a compact attention surface but only its body exclusion has been proven
  + Justification: exact paired byte measurement tests whether projection actually compresses the tool result and bounds the claim to serialized fixtures
  + Solution: generate validate serialize and publish paired inspect-versus-resolve measurements across all twelve registry entries

& [Delineation]
  + inspect-response byte size is distinct from query size full checkpoint size model tokens runtime memory and latency
  + pairing the same handle and root isolates result-surface choice from registry identity
  + full resolve remains necessary whenever a host requires complete state
  + provider-free fixtures establish no live tool-call compatibility

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + ordered case identity includes ordinal phase position terminal flag checkpoint digest and all four byte counts
